# Concurrent-job caps per node for the carbon auto-submitters (slurm/auto_submit_specs.sh,
# slurm/auto_submit_carbon.sh). SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# Edit a value here and the RUNNING submitter picks it up within one poll cycle — NO restart needed
# (the submitters re-read this file each loop iteration). Integers only; values above the node's
# physical GPU count are clamped (laniakea has 8 GPUs, voyager 4) for safety. Lines must be exactly
# `NAME=INT` (the parser ignores anything else, falling back to the defaults 7 / 3).
# laniakea (8 GPUs) / voyager (4 GPUs) / galaxy (3090s — hosts the SSD). Set GAL_CAP>0 to also use
# galaxy (NOTE: galaxy jobs need node-local SSD paths — handled in carbon_distill.sbatch).
LAN_CAP=7
VOY_CAP=4
GAL_CAP=4
